cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this code, cite Godot Engine and the org fork it is vendored from.
title: Godot core subset for curvenet.elf (vendored)
abstract: >-
  42 source files of the org's Godot fork (entities-godot) plus its
  LICENSE.txt, 484,310 bytes before this file: the math, containers and
  Curve3D that Cassie's pen -> curvenet -> mesh path calls, so it runs in a
  sandbox guest with no engine. Taken: core/typedefs.h,
  core/error/error_list.h; core/math/{math_defs.h, math_funcs.{h,cpp},
  math_funcs_binary.h, vector2.{h,cpp}, vector2i.{h,cpp}, vector3.{h,cpp},
  vector3i.{h,cpp}, basis.{h,cpp}, quaternion.{h,cpp}, transform_3d.{h,cpp},
  plane.{h,cpp}, aabb.{h,cpp}, dynamic_bvh.{h,cpp}, geometry_3d.{h,cpp}};
  core/templates/{hashfuncs.{h,cpp}, hash_map.h, hash_set.h, local_vector.h,
  pair.h, sort_array.h, sort_list.h, list.h, paged_allocator.h, rb_map.h,
  span.h}; scene/resources/curve.{h,cpp}. What they include from the rest
  of Godot (memory, error macros, String, Vector, Variant, Object,
  Resource) is the hand-written guest/godot_lite, at the same include
  paths. tools/vendor/godot_core_subset.py reproduces the tree from the
  pinned commit; every edit asserts how many times its anchor matches.
  Local adaptations:
  (1) every file's body, below its includes, is wrapped in namespace gdl,
  so nothing collides with the godot-sandbox guest API in the same ELF;
  (2) the explicit operator String() declarations and definitions are
  removed from vector2, vector2i, vector3, vector3i, basis, quaternion,
  transform_3d, plane and aabb, and the 18 error messages that printed a
  value through it print a fixed placeholder such as "<p_normal>" instead;
  (3) the Variant-returning *_bind helpers are removed from plane (3) and
  aabb (2), with their core/variant/variant.h includes;
  (4) math_funcs.cpp loses the RandomPCG-backed rand_from_seed, seed,
  randomize, rand, randfn and the three random overloads, and the
  random_pcg.h include (Cassie draws no random numbers);
  (5) geometry_3d.{h,cpp} keep only get_closest_points_between_segments,
  the one Geometry3D function Cassie calls;
  (6) curve.{h,cpp} keep only Curve3D (curve.cpp from get_point_count
  through the constructor, lines 1363-2398 at the pin), without its
  PropertyListHelper members, the _set/_get/_get_property_list/
  _property_can_revert/_property_get_revert forwarders, _filter_property
  and _bind_methods; the constructor body is empty;
  (7) each file except LICENSE.txt starts with a one-line banner naming
  the pin and the script.
type: software
